WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A readable view helps us inspect
the model without confusing

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.220 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
presentation with analysis.

3
00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:09.440 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Start with the FireSat tutorial
tree in the light Parchment view.

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:15.060 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Use Find node or HID to locate
a card, Focus to center it,

5
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.720 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and Fit tree to recover
the overall structure.

6
00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:19.080 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Open Properties.

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.560 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Node properties and Attack
metrics are separate groups.

8
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.800 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Show Node ID, Authoritative
UUID, and Provenance,

9
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.700 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then select only the metrics
needed for this review.

10
00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:34.780 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The title, type, and HID remain
recognizable even when optional rows are

11
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.940 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
hidden from the cards.

12
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.280 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Node ID identifies an
element within this tree.

13
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.400 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The HID is its readable Core identifier;

14
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.820 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Authoritative UUID identifies
its authoritative record.

15
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.180 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A newly staged attack shows not yet
committed until a successful Core

16
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.040 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
transaction assigns its identity.

17
00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:58.020 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A shared node keeps one identity even
when several relationships lead to it.

18
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.540 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Close the dialog and use Auto-arrange.

19
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.100 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Try the Direction choices
Top down and Left to right.

20
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.620 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
These choices and manual card
movement change the presentation.

21
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.640 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
They do not change gates,
sequence positions, raw inputs,

22
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
or the calculated meaning of the analysis.

23
00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.700 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Roll up a branch, inspect its folded
marker, and roll it down again.

24
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.940 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Hidden descendants still participate
in calculations and capacity limits.

25
00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Tailored out is different: it excludes
a relationship from analytical

26
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.360 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
traversal and requires a reason.

27
00:01:29.527 --> 00:01:33.640 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Use folding to manage clutter, not to
claim that an attack has disappeared.

28
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.800 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
At the upper right of the canvas,
select Nocturne for dark mode,

29
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then Parchment to return.

30
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.580 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This changes presentation only.
